* pt_ptrim: generated by analog/wired_rx/netlists.py -- do not edit by hand
* AC-3 per-phase delay trim between the RX pt_pll_ring PH0..7 and the slicer/capture CKP0..7, r10 (2026-11-18,
* MW-14: sized for the real clock loads, 0.98 pF on CKP0 and 0.37-0.48 pF on CKP1..7).
* Channel: NAND(PHk, ptrim_en) 2 x (4, 6) -> tn -> inv1 4/8 -> ta -> inv2 4 x 4/8 -> tb -> inv3 10 x 5/10 -> CKPk
* (non-inverting).  5-bit binary trim T{k}_4..0 = cdr.phase_trim[k]: switched NMOS gate capacitors, bits 0 and 1 on
* tn only (1 and 2 units), bits 2..4 split 2+2 / 4+4 / 8+8 units between tn and ta so that CKP rise and fall move
* alike (duty independent of the code); unit widths per bit are tuned on the extraction for binary weights.
* Channel 0 carries the capture's main clock: inv1 / inv2 / inv3 doubled and its ta units twice as wide; channels
* 1..7 carry a dummy inv1 gate (MOS capacitors to the rails) on tn instead.  ptrim_en=0: every CKPk low.
* r12: channel k also carries PTRIM_FIX[k] always-on unit pairs (bit-4 type, switch gate ptrim_en) = a fixed delay
* offset cancelling the systematic phase-position pattern of the RX ring pt_pll_ring r12 (TIM-19), so the 5-bit trim
* only has to cover the residual, the channel / sampler spread and die mismatch.
* Calibrated per board from edge-sampler histograms (digital).  Requirement: step <= 1 deg, monotonic, range
* covering the ring's static phase position error plus the channel spread (spec AC-3: residual <= 3 deg).
.subckt pt_ptrim VDD_WIRE_SW VSS ptrim_en PH0 PH1 PH2 PH3 PH4 PH5 PH6 PH7 CKP0 CKP1 CKP2 CKP3 CKP4 CKP5 CKP6 CKP7 T0_0 T0_1 T0_2 T0_3 T0_4 T1_0 T1_1 T1_2 T1_3 T1_4 T2_0 T2_1 T2_2 T2_3 T2_4 T3_0 T3_1 T3_2 T3_3 T3_4 T4_0 T4_1 T4_2 T4_3 T4_4 T5_0 T5_1 T5_2 T5_3 T5_4 T6_0 T6_1 T6_2 T6_3 T6_4 T7_0 T7_1 T7_2 T7_3 T7_4
XMN1 tn0_s0 PH0 VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=4u l=0.28u
XMN2 tn0 ptrim_en tn0_s0 VSS nfet_03v3 w=4u l=0.28u
XMN3 tn0_s1 PH0 VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=4u l=0.28u
XMN4 tn0 ptrim_en tn0_s1 VSS nfet_03v3 w=4u l=0.28u
